WARNING:ENOSYS: ENOSYS means 'invalid syscall nr' and nothing else
#285: FILE: tools/testing/selftests/membarrier/membarrier_test2.c:158:
+		if (errno == ENOSYS)

ENOSYS means that a nonexistent system call was called.
Earlier, it was wrongly used for things like invalid operations on
otherwise valid syscalls.  This should be avoided in new code.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/5eb299021dec23c1a48fa7d9f2c8b794e967766d.1408730669.git.luto@amacapital.net/

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'mbt[i].command > 0'
#292: FILE: tools/testing/selftests/membarrier/membarrier_test2.c:165:
+		if ((mbt[i].command > 0) && (ret & mbt[i].command))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

